./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0017/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:317:./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0013/committee2/systems_reviewer.err:1386:RATIONALE: RED. The claimed systems insight requires committed tool-result spans that are cold under H2O shortly after commit and hot only later. The packet's L1 directly refutes that mechanism: critical handle spans are heavy-hitters from commit, attention rank rises 0.50->1.00, H2O future-ref AUC is 0.999/0.819 overall and 1.000 on critical handles, while the lexical proxy is weaker at 0.857/0.647. End-to-end, CAUSAL gives no advantage over H2O: +0.00 [0,0] at all budgets. Prior art and OSS also leave no defensible systems-design contribution: H2O implements heavy-hitter eviction, OpenVINO GenAI ships attention-score KV eviction including SnapKV/KVCrush, SGLang/TensorRT-LLM/LMCache ship KV reuse/retention/eviction infrastructure, and ArkVale/Quest-style prior work covers query-aware or recallable recovery of later-important KV without lexical handles. The residual lexical tool-span signal is glue, and in the measured workload it is redundant with H2O.
