<section id="welcome-to-lmcache">
<h1>Welcome to LMCache!<a @click.prevent="window.navigator.clipboard.writeText($el.href); $el.setAttribute('data-tooltip', 'Copied!'); setTimeout(() =&gt; $el.setAttribute('data-tooltip', 'Copy link to this element'), 2000)" aria-label="Copy link to this element" class="headerlink" data-tooltip="Copy link to this element" href="#welcome-to-lmcache"><span>#</span></a></h1>
<img alt="LMCache" class="no-scaled-link" src="_images/lmcache-logo_crop.png" style="width: 60%;"/>
<strong> Supercharge Your LLM with the Fastest KV Cache Layer. </strong>
<a aria-label="Star" class="github-button" data-show-count="true" data-size="large" href="https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache">Star</a>
<a aria-label="Watch" class="github-button" data-icon="octicon-eye" data-size="large" href="https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/subscription">Watch</a>
<a aria-label="Fork" class="github-button" data-icon="octicon-repo-forked" data-show-count="true" data-size="large" href="https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/fork">Fork</a>
LMCache lets LLMs prefill each text only once. By storing the KV caches of all reusable texts, LMCache can reuse the KV caches of any reused text (not necessarily prefix) in any serving engine instance.
By combining LMCache with vLLM, LMCaches achieves 3-10x delay savings and GPU cycle reduction in many LLM use cases, including multi-round QA and RAG.
<li><p><a class="reference external" href="https://lmcache.github.io">LMCache blogs</a></p></li>
<li><p><a class="reference external" href="https://join.slack.com/t/lmcacheworkspace/shared_invite/zt-3eck2v8ub-j2hPn0AdzcfyykatTBXSTg">Join LMCache slack workspace</a></p></li>
<li><p><a class="reference external" href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3651890.3672274">CacheGen: KV Cache Compression and Streaming for Fast Large Language Model Serving</a></p></li>
<li><p><a class="reference external" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.16444">CacheBlend: Fast Large Language Model Serving with Cached Knowledge Fusion</a></p></li>
<p class="caption" role="heading"><span class="caption-text">Welcome to LMCache</span></p>
